<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Operational Task Planning">
  <data key="d0">Operational Task Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Operational Task Planning is a systematic process involving planning, preparation, and implementation to achieve operational objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Task Planning is a core methodology for organizing and commanding combat operations, covering planning, preparation, and implementation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Task Planning is the process of organizing and designing military operations, involving commanders, staff, and professional planners.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-635858509e41f8078abbb43649372ec8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03367b3f7f20f2a9f77e53026ed67d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-planning">
  <data key="d0">Pre-planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-planning lays the foundation for pre-combat planning and requires careful formulation to prepare commanders for future situations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-combat Planning">
  <data key="d0">Pre-combat Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-combat Planning involves the revision of pre-planning and serves as an adjustment and supplement based on battlefield conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-combat Planning Control">
  <data key="d0">In-combat Planning Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">In-combat Planning Control refers to the real-time regulation of troop actions during operations to adapt to changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Task Planning System">
  <data key="d0">Task Planning System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Task Planning System is a technical support tool that enables efficient campaign design and plan formulation using models and data.&lt;SEP&gt;Task planning system refers to the various level and type of mission planning systems used flexibly in developing combat plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commanders">
  <data key="d0">Commanders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Commanders are responsible for making operational decisions and require support from planning systems to complete the OODA loop.&lt;SEP&gt;Military leaders who make operational decisions and rely on staff and planning systems during the planning process.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders are military leaders who analyze battlefield conditions and make strategic decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d95a5040be8056ebebc1096496f2b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Staff Team">
  <data key="d0">Staff Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Staff team collaborates with commanders in campaign tactical planning to form battlefield judgments and overall concepts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Staff Team works with commanders and professional units to utilize planning tools for operational control.&lt;SEP&gt;Staff Team is the group that conducts operational task planning, including mission analysis, situation assessment, auxiliary concept design, operational plan development, wargaming evaluation, action plan preparation, and action order generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Staff team assists the commander in analyzing battlefield situations and combat missions, developing combat plans, and executing planning tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Staff team consists of military personnel who assist commanders in planning and evaluating operational plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Staff Team is a group of military professionals who receive enemy action plan evaluation explanations and ranking lists to support decision-making.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444624ac7ec860ede259c10c50f0513a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-761ebe6109f1660d08131cf4842e3809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a38c5d2bd5aded4f705e8a27f80c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659db68304082ade8ac85e6762c422cb</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire Strike Operation">
  <data key="d0">Fire Strike Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire Strike Operation is a type of campaign offensive operation style that serves as a typical demonstration for other operation styles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strategic Security Environment">
  <data key="d0">Strategic Security Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Strategic Security Environment includes political, economic, military, and diplomatic factors that influence operational task planning.&lt;SEP&gt;The strategic security environment involves war potential and core interests such as sovereignty and strategic benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5234e8dd3cbe0a809d3d59ad862a11</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Friendly And Enemy Force Resources">
  <data key="d0">Friendly And Enemy Force Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Friendly And Enemy Force Resources consist of the combat forces of all parties involved and are a key factor in planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OODA Loop">
  <data key="d0">OODA Loop</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Observe-Orient-Decide-Act cycle used in In-war Plan regulation for fire strike operations and effect judgment.&lt;SEP&gt;The OODA Loop represents the engagement process of observation, orientation, decision, and action that planning systems aim to complete faster than the enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;OODA Loop refers to the Observe-Orient-Decide-Act decision-making cycle used in military strategy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b0ab60a625810ad5c7b928b03f9f35b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92553208105fab6dba3a8603376ed607</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Planning">
  <data key="d0">Operational Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional concept described as creative thinking activity by senior commanders based on experience and new situations.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Planning is the core of forming campaign guidance and involves prediction, shaping, and adaptation.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of planning military operations, reflecting command art and military thought, occurring before joint operational plan formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Planning is the core process of defining and solving operational problems through design and方案formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Planning is the cyclic process of understanding strategic intent, leading campaign design, conducting wargaming evaluation, and supervising task planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-761ebe6109f1660d08131cf4842e3809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-112dc88d3b89a6b06ab8767eb54ad739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a38c5d2bd5aded4f705e8a27f80c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc498b8576e8ab1b2cbded8e3f1ca004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Situation Prediction">
  <data key="d0">Situation Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Situation Prediction is the premise of scientific decision-making, using objective information to deduce natural development trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Situation Shaping">
  <data key="d0">Situation Shaping</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Situation Shaping is key to grasping battlefield initiative by expanding active influence over crises.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Action Adaptation">
  <data key="d0">Action Adaptation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Action Adaptation ensures control over battlefield changes by helping troops adapt to or utilize uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battlefield Natural Environment">
  <data key="d0">Battlefield Natural Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Battlefield Natural Environment is a factor that must be comprehensively considered in operational task planning.&lt;SEP&gt;The battlefield natural environment includes geography, weather, ocean, and network electromagnetic conditions affecting operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5234e8dd3cbe0a809d3d59ad862a11</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Social Human Environment">
  <data key="d0">Social Human Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Social Human Environment is a factor influencing operational task planning alongside strategic and force resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The social human environment involves politics, economy, law, culture, and religion affecting war motives and outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5234e8dd3cbe0a809d3d59ad862a11</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Professional Units">
  <data key="d0">Professional Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Professional Units work alongside commanders and staff teams to utilize planning tools for operational control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Design">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Design</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign Design is a part of the Commander's planning, involving forming overall concepts and finding solutions to key problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Design is the core of Concept Design, converting decision thinking into determination and will.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Design is efficiently completed with the support of the task planning system during operation planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Design involves determining campaign objectives, operational guidelines, and designing the operational process and force composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Design refers to the process of planning campaign operations, incorporating operational methods to achieve operational purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Design is the core process of forming campaign concepts, involving the systematic analysis of enemy situations, friendly situations, and battlefield environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign design is the core of campaign concept formation, involving guidance and development of joint operations concepts to provide thought and methodological guidance for combat planning and mission planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-112dc88d3b89a6b06ab8767eb54ad739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9aa65c773b4ac4c1207cd5361f531e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a38c5d2bd5aded4f705e8a27f80c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-635858509e41f8078abbb43649372ec8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03367b3f7f20f2a9f77e53026ed67d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operation Plan">
  <data key="d0">Operation Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operation Plan includes overall plans, branch plans, and task instructions generated during fire strike operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Operation plan refers to the comprehensive document that outlines combat objectives, strategies, and execution procedures for military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Operation Plan is the detailed planning document that outlines specific combat actions, timelines, and resource allocation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38d3c5592e48544d872c05c7c8f83f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79ee866bec5531e5d971890f7a2559fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human-in-the-loop">
  <data key="d0">Human-in-the-loop</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Human-in-the-loop is the basic usage mode for task planning in fire strike operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Discovery">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Discovery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge Discovery is a tool utilized by the task planning system based on models and data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Algorithm Analysis Tools">
  <data key="d0">Algorithm Analysis Tools</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Algorithm Analysis Tools are used by the task planning system to complete planning and action control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Political Purpose">
  <data key="d0">Political Purpose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Political Purpose is the primary factor of war within the strategic security environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="War Potential">
  <data key="d0">War Potential</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">War Potential is a factor involved in the strategic security environment.&lt;SEP&gt;War Potential is a metric used in firepower damage assessment, where a decrease of 50% may be a standard indicator.&lt;SEP&gt;War potential is a factor involved in the strategic security environment affecting national core interests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bacfc6aae6b44233cca3776c36497ebe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5234e8dd3cbe0a809d3d59ad862a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c6573c8c574cef431bea4de45d41a77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evolutionary Deduction">
  <data key="d0">Evolutionary Deduction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Evolutionary deduction is a method for transforming military campaign planning into a visualized action path with clear主线and脉络(main lines and context).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visualized Campaign Action Path">
  <data key="d0">Visualized Campaign Action Path</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visualized campaign action path refers to the visualized battle action path derived from evolutionary deduction, which has clear主线and脉络.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Operation Start And End State">
  <data key="d0">Combat Operation Start And End State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat operation start and end state refers to the clear definition of starting and ending conditions for combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Mission And Action Deduction">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Mission And Action Deduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign mission and action deduction is the process of analyzing main combat missions and designing supporting combat actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Process Design">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Process Design</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign process design involves correlating and integrating all combat actions to extract main and key combat actions as components of the campaign implementation main line.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Process Design refers to the planning and structuring of the campaign timeline and phases.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign process design involves dividing campaign into stages and planning the sequence and timing of combat actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Process Design involves planning and structuring the sequence of military operations over time, including main attacks, secondary attacks, and defensive actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign process design involves planning the sequence and phases of military operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b76b9404888b1ba7ea6890ea44e06497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phase Mission And Action Deduction">
  <data key="d0">Phase Mission And Action Deduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase mission and action deduction involves deducing tasks and actions for different phases of the campaign.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Force Usage And Task Allocation">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Force Usage And Task Allocation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign force usage and task allocation refers to the allocation of campaign forces and assignment of tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy">
  <data key="d0">Enemy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy is the opposing force whose operational intentions are analyzed, whose action plans are assumed, and whose advantages and disadvantages are evaluated.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy refers to the opposing forces whose possible actions and strategies are deduced through linear reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;The enemy refers to the opposing force in combat operations, whose possible actions or strategies form the basis for sub-action task division.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy refers to adversarial forces whose intentions, capabilities, and activities need to be analyzed through intelligence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e076ff2b14def31d05c594776649eee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Reasoning Method">
  <data key="d0">Linear Reasoning Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Linear reasoning method is used to归纳(induce) and propose various actions or strategies that the enemy might adopt.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Mission Correlation Model">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Mission Correlation Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign mission correlation model is constructed by sorting out the main combat missions and their correlation and support relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Forces">
  <data key="d0">Combat Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat forces are the military units selected and constructed through dynamic confrontation games for conducting combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat forces refer to the main combat forces involved in combat actions, including their composition and organizational structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat forces refer to the military units and personnel engaged in combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad0e7eab09ee2232d2cf67519d5dbb8</data>
