<node id="Campaign Concept">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Concept</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign concept is the overall conception of combat operations and solutions to key problems, formed through careful thinking and logical reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Concept refers to the core idea or vision formed during campaign design, representing the central concept around which operational planning revolves.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign concept is the strategic framework developed based on task analysis to guide operational execution.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign concept refers to the overall conception of the campaign formed through mission and action deduction and process design.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign concept is the final confirmation of combat action start/end states, campaign task and action divisions, campaign process design, task lists, and task allocation, submitted for superior approval.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign concept is the initial idea proposed by the commander that guides plan development.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign concept refers to the strategic vision and framework that guides the development of operational plans during the second phase of pre-war revision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43ccfe322d45a2193b169b151539c560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a38c5d2bd5aded4f705e8a27f80c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30f82772b0d833e6eb3891686c80b3f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f5b0f0bcf4f17a0423f4bb55586b580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79ee866bec5531e5d971890f7a2559fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
