  <data key="d2">Battlefield space refers to the operational environment including ground, sea, air, and even low-orbit space targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Battlefield Space refers to the geographic and operational area where military activities occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad0e7eab09ee2232d2cf67519d5dbb8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Attack Action">
  <data key="d0">Main Attack Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Main Attack Action represents the primary offensive operation that an enemy might undertake in a campaign.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Attack Action">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Attack Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary Attack Action represents supporting offensive operations that complement the main attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense Action">
  <data key="d0">Defense Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Defense Action refers to protective military operations an enemy might employ.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign Nodes are key time and geographic space nodes for important operations, revised based on enemy and friendly combat operation deduction results.&lt;SEP&gt;Campaign Nodes are critical points or milestones in a campaign that require support and coordination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d621707561f0a7571c7fbe5d409dfa37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Reconnaissance">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Reconnaissance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intelligence Reconnaissance is the activity of collecting information about the enemy, which forms the basis for determining the center of gravity but may be hindered by enemy deception and battlefield camouflage.&lt;SEP&gt;Intelligence reconnaissance is the systematic process of collecting, analyzing, and distributing intelligence information about enemies and battlefield conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intelligence Reconnaissance is the systematic process of gathering information about enemy forces and battlefield conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intelligence reconnaissance involves gathering information about enemy fleet size, vessel types, target positions, coordinates, speed, and heading.&lt;SEP&gt;Intelligence reconnaissance is the process of collecting intelligence information to determine whether it meets standards for prediction, timeliness, accuracy, availability, completeness, relevance, objectivity, and usability.&lt;SEP&gt;Intelligence Reconnaissance involves gathering, analyzing, and distributing information about enemy activities and the operational environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38d3c5592e48544d872c05c7c8f83f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2908bfab4991ca36f91164f7b6393526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a38c5d2bd5aded4f705e8a27f80c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dec14ab6a6d09aebc156102953b5c47d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79ee866bec5531e5d971890f7a2559fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Combat Actions">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Combat Actions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy Combat Actions are all possible combat operations that the enemy might take, predicted through forward-looking reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy Combat Actions refer to the decomposed tactical tasks, types, and strategies that make up enemy combat plans, including deployment areas, attack directions, and objectives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d621707561f0a7571c7fbe5d409dfa37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third-Party Countries">
  <data key="d0">Third-Party Countries</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Third-Party Countries refer to nations other than the primary belligerents that might provide cooperation or support to either side.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Allies">
  <data key="d0">Allies</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Allies are nations or forces that cooperate and provide mutual support in military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Allies are partner nations or forces that cooperate politically, militarily, and economically with a country.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Our Forces">
  <data key="d0">Our Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Our Forces represents the military unit conducting the planning and analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Missions">
  <data key="d0">Combat Missions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Missions are specific tasks assigned to military units during operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Methods">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Methods</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical Methods refer to the specific techniques and procedures used in combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feasibility">
  <data key="d0">Feasibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Feasibility is an evaluation criterion used to assess whether target strikes and combat operations can be successfully accomplished.&lt;SEP&gt;Feasibility refers to the practicality of executing a combat scenario based on timing and conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Feasibility refers to the measure of how possible and practical it is for the enemy to implement a particular combat plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d621707561f0a7571c7fbe5d409dfa37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Possibility">
  <data key="d0">Possibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Possibility refers to the likelihood or probability of the enemy adopting a specific combat plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Degree">
  <data key="d0">Support Degree</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Support Degree refers to the level of resources, logistics, and backing available to support the enemy's combat plan execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Threat Level">
  <data key="d0">Threat Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Threat Level refers to the degree of danger and potential impact posed by the enemy's combat plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptability">
  <data key="d0">Adaptability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptability refers to the degree to which an enemy combat plan can adjust to changing battlefield conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uniqueness">
  <data key="d0">Uniqueness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Uniqueness refers to distinctive or unusual characteristics of a combat scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;Uniqueness refers to the distinctive characteristics that differentiate one enemy combat plan from others.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency">
  <data key="d0">Consistency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistency is an evaluation criterion used to assess alignment between target strikes, combat objectives, and expected situations.&lt;SEP&gt;Consistency refers to alignment between combat scenarios and existing enemy doctrines and tactics.&lt;SEP&gt;Consistency refers to the coherence and logical alignment of an enemy combat plan across different operational aspects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d621707561f0a7571c7fbe5d409dfa37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unexpected Actions">
  <data key="d0">Unexpected Actions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unexpected Actions refer to surprise moves or unconventional strategies the enemy might employ.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Strategies">
  <data key="d0">Special Strategies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Special Strategies refer to unconventional or exceptional tactics the enemy might use to gain advantage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk">
  <data key="d0">Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk is an evaluation criterion used to assess potential negative outcomes and uncertainties of target strikes and combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk refers to potential negative outcomes or vulnerabilities in combat plan execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d621707561f0a7571c7fbe5d409dfa37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key Influencing Factors">
  <data key="d0">Key Influencing Factors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Key Influencing Factors refer to critical elements that significantly affect the outcome of enemy combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Counter-Attack">
  <data key="d0">Counter-Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Counter-Attack refers to offensive actions taken by the enemy in response to defensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Center Of Gravity">
  <data key="d0">Combat Center Of Gravity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat center of gravity is the key point analyzed during campaign concept design, representing the source of combat capability.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat Center Of Gravity refers to the enemy's primary source of strength or critical vulnerability in operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deception Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Deception Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deception Strategy refers to misleading tactics the enemy might employ, such as feigned attacks or covert maneuvers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Habits">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Habits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical Habits refer to the enemy's traditional or常规patterns of combat behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Action Model">
  <data key="d0">Action Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Action Model refers to a framework representing the enemy's typical operational patterns and behaviors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ability Model">
  <data key="d0">Ability Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ability Model refers to a framework representing the enemy's combat capabilities and limitations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental Model">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental Model refers to a framework representing how battlefield conditions affect operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sub-Action List">
  <data key="d0">Sub-Action List</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-Action List refers to the detailed breakdown of component actions within an enemy combat plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deceptive Actions">
  <data key="d0">Deceptive Actions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deceptive Actions refer to enemy operations designed to mislead, confuse, or create false impressions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Constraints">
  <data key="d0">Operational Constraints</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operational Constraints refer to limitations and restrictions that affect the execution of combat plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Operations">
  <data key="d0">Combat Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat operations are influenced by natural and social environments and involve target strikes and force deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat operations refer to all supportive, auxiliary, support, and guarantee actions and tasks related to military operations, serving as the starting point for forming action task game trees.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat Operations are the main and auxiliary support actions that are decomposed and revised, including coordination and cooperation between operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat operations encompass the three stages of planning, decision-making, and command, requiring intelligence support throughout.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5234e8dd3cbe0a809d3d59ad862a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e076ff2b14def31d05c594776649eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d621707561f0a7571c7fbe5d409dfa37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766696</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sub-Action Tasks">
  <data key="d0">Sub-Action Tasks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-action tasks are subdivisions of combat operations based on factors such as participating forces, operational attributes, and operational areas. They include all supportive, auxiliary, support, and guarantee actions related to combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Action Task Game Tree">
  <data key="d0">Action Task Game Tree</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Action task game tree is a structured decision tree formed based on combat operations, representing the hierarchical relationship of tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Armed Forces">
  <data key="d0">Armed Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Armed forces refer to various military branches (army, navy, air force) or combat sub-centers responsible for evaluating the feasibility, effectiveness, and reliability of sub-action tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Reasoning Chain Method">
  <data key="d0">Linear Reasoning Chain Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Linear reasoning chain method is used to infer enemy actions by decomposing and summarizing possible enemy actions based on probable campaign operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Action Inference">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Action Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy action inference involves decomposing enemy probable operations, summarizing possible actions or strategies, and proposing countermeasures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy-Us Confrontation Deduction">
  <data key="d0">Enemy-Us Confrontation Deduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy-us confrontation deduction analyzes the enemy's most probable combat actions and their probabilities, using calculation models and decision trees to examine the comprehensiveness, feasibility, and effectiveness of combat action designs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Logical Line">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Logical Line</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Campaign logical line effectively connects campaign actions, time, locations, and purposes to form a physical logic line describing campaign operational ideas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strike Target Nomination List">
  <data key="d0">Strike Target Nomination List</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Strike target nomination list is formed based on campaign process design and combat action inference results, combined with enemy analysis conclusions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Formation">
  <data key="d0">Combat Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Formation refers to organized military units that carry out combat missions and operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat formation defines the composition of combat forces and command coordination relationships based on campaign action stages and enemy action inference results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67849e0b5328f68ea35509bd6b19645b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Grouping">
  <data key="d0">Combat Grouping</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat grouping is further refined based on combat formation, task lists, enemy-us confrontation conclusions, and tactics design to ensure successful execution of sub-action tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Troop Resources">
  <data key="d0">Troop Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
