<node id="Combat Capability">
  <data key="d0">Combat Capability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Capability refers to the operational ability of forces, analyzed during force planning and enemy threat analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat capability refers to the military capabilities of enemy forces, analyzed during enemy action inference.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat capability refers to the overall ability of military forces to conduct effective combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat capability refers to the enemy's military abilities and strengths that must be assessed through intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat capability refers to the ability to conduct military operations, including offensive and defensive strengths.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad0e7eab09ee2232d2cf67519d5dbb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e076ff2b14def31d05c594776649eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c6573c8c574cef431bea4de45d41a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac85adc8a2b85efe002961c570418c8</data>
