<node id="Target Selection">
  <data key="d0">Target Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Target selection follows the logic of strategic intent to campaign objectives and identifies high-value targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Target Selection is the process of revising combat missions, compiling target nomination lists, analyzing and selecting strike targets, and evaluating feasibility, risk, and consistency to form a joint target strike list.&lt;SEP&gt;Target selection refers to the process of choosing打击目标during pre-war plan revision, determining which enemy assets or positions will be attacked.&lt;SEP&gt;Target selection is a traditional planning activity for identifying appropriate objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Target selection is the process of identifying and choosing specific enemy objectives for attack operations.</data>
