<node id="Pre-Planning">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-planning is a planning approach developed during peacetime based on analysis of strategic situations to effectively respond to potential war threats in major strategic directions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-planning refers to the advance planning process conducted before operational execution.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-planning is conducted during peacetime to develop combat concepts, plans, and contingency plans based on combat intentions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-planning is conducted during peacetime to develop combat concepts, schemes, and plans based on operational intentions.</data>
