</node>
<node id="Multiple Contingency Plans">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Contingency Plans</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiple contingency plans refer to the principle of preparing several alternative plans for potential war scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bafe3365a36fae45b1bf2e0446eac189</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multiple Means Preparation">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Means Preparation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiple means preparation refers to preparing various operational methods and resources for a single type of action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bafe3365a36fae45b1bf2e0446eac189</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Situation Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Situation Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Situation assessment is a functional process in pre-planning that involves analyzing and judging the strategic situation.&lt;SEP&gt;Situation Assessment is one of three fundamental tasks in operational planning, involving analysis of enemy situation, our own situation, and battlefield environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Situation Assessment involves analyzing operational conditions and progress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bafe3365a36fae45b1bf2e0446eac189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b76b9404888b1ba7ea6890ea44e06497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Situational Awareness">
  <data key="d0">Situational Awareness</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Situational awareness is a functional process in pre-combat planning that involves perceiving and understanding the current operational environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Situational awareness refers to the real-time understanding of battlefield conditions, enemy positions, and operational status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bafe3365a36fae45b1bf2e0446eac189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e076ff2b14def31d05c594776649eee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plan Execution">
  <data key="d0">Plan Execution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Plan execution is a functional process specific to pre-combat planning, involving the implementation of developed plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bafe3365a36fae45b1bf2e0446eac189</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Task Planning">
  <data key="d0">Task Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Task planning is a process that focuses on selecting strike target groups, determining strike sequences, defining combat missions, and establishing earliest/latest strike times based on combat intent, enemy and friendly situations, and effectiveness data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Intent">
  <data key="d0">Combat Intent</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat intent refers to the operational purpose and goals of military planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat Intent refers to the commander's understanding of objectives, timelines, and operational approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat intent refers to the enemy's intended actions and purposes that must be analyzed through intelligence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e076ff2b14def31d05c594776649eee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy And Friendly Situations">
  <data key="d0">Enemy And Friendly Situations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy and friendly situations include air defense radar deployment, major airports, air-to-ground missile positions, main airspace, rendezvous point settings, and descriptions of strike/suppression target characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battlefield Environment">
  <data key="d0">Battlefield Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Battlefield Environment is the set of physical, operational, and situational conditions and circumstances in which military operations occur. It encompasses the geographical context—including terrain, weather, and natural features—as well as the broader operational environment, such as the main campaign directions, that shape how forces can maneuver and engage. In addition to the physical landscape, the battlefield environment includes all electromagnetic and external factors that influence combat, ranging from communication and electronic warfare conditions to the presence of favorable or unfavorable elements that affect tactical decisions.

The environment is not static; it includes dynamic enemy and friendly situations that change in real time, requiring continuous updates to planning and decision‑making. As a key factor in situation judgment, the Battlefield Environment is analyzed alongside enemy and friendly dispositions to understand its impact on operational actions. It serves as a primary focus of intelligence collection, providing the situational awareness necessary for effective combat operations and ensuring that commanders can adapt their strategies to evolving conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-461d0fe22701b4d81bbb3d49249308a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b76b9404888b1ba7ea6890ea44e06497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9aa65c773b4ac4c1207cd5361f531e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a38c5d2bd5aded4f705e8a27f80c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e076ff2b14def31d05c594776649eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c868520f6a3dc6f1e022369db6d23482&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03367b3f7f20f2a9f77e53026ed67d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac85adc8a2b85efe002961c570418c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Effectiveness Data">
  <data key="d0">Effectiveness Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Effectiveness data refers to assessments of combat capabilities of both sides, including penetration probabilities of various aircraft types and forces needed to strike different targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strike Target Groups">
  <data key="d0">Strike Target Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strike target groups are collections of targets selected for attack during combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Cover Formation">
  <data key="d0">Air Cover Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Air cover formation is primarily composed of fighter aviation and is responsible for providing protective coverage through screening air patrol, air escort, air interception, air hunting, air blockade, and air cover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fighter Aviation">
  <data key="d0">Fighter Aviation</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Fighter aviation refers to the enemy fighter aircraft units with strong combat capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Fighter aviation is the military aviation force responsible for air cover operations, including interception and escort missions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0d1b6a8aabc98d09750deaec7618bb</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
