<node id="Combat Mission">
  <data key="d0">Combat Mission</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Mission refers to the specific tasks assigned to combat forces as part of military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat Mission refers to the military task to be accomplished, including basic tasks, specified tasks, and implied tasks, determined by mission nature, importance, interrelationships, and execution sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat mission refers to the specific tasks and objectives to be accomplished during military operations, including pre-planned, new, and implied missions.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat mission refers to the specific tactical tasks assigned to formations to accomplish objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat mission refers to specific military tasks that need to be accomplished during warfare, which may be added or terminated based on operational assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ea72184694bbe0bd0d0c0b30a73271&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67849e0b5328f68ea35509bd6b19645b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a38c5d2bd5aded4f705e8a27f80c90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79ee866bec5531e5d971890f7a2559fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766711</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Plan">
  <data key="d0">Combat Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Plan is a comprehensive military planning document that serves as the detailed operational framework for warfare. It functions as the transformation of the commander's campaign concept into executable plans, incorporating critical elements such as assumptions about enemy actions, task allocation, force deployment, combat action planning, coordination methods, and combat time calculation. This planning document provides the overall arrangement and specific design for armed service combat operations, forming a complete plan system that guides military campaign execution.

The Combat Plan includes multiple pre-positioned plans and various means of preparation, serving as a complete operational plan generated through the systematic planning process. It细化 (elaborates) and implements the campaign concept, completing the details of combat actions and task implementation. The document encompasses strategic objectives and tactical approaches, includes options and response measures, and covers the operational scheme developed during mission planning for executing attacks. In naval contexts, it may specifically address comprehensive schemes for executing sea-to-sea and sea-to-land strikes. Additionally, the Combat Plan provides the overall plan for military operations, incorporating progress assessment and task execution evaluation to ensure operational effectiveness and adaptability throughout campaign execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e101ad5b001673244e87b269cca1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bafe3365a36fae45b1bf2e0446eac189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38d3c5592e48544d872c05c7c8f83f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ea72184694bbe0bd0d0c0b30a73271&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b265ec00b234e282f6fbd72461d3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659db68304082ade8ac85e6762c422cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f5b0f0bcf4f17a0423f4bb55586b580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc4c1f92f953300c7b9ad35242864ff7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766711</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suppression Method">
  <data key="d0">Suppression Method</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suppression method refers to the specific approach used to neutralize or degrade enemy air defense capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52002d5c447b3c7fdbb3908a46c355ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766711</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
