  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="北约国家">
  <data key="d0">北约国家</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">北约国家是北大西洋公约组织的成员国，部分北约国家追捧系统作战设计方法。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="基于效果作战理论">
  <data key="d0">基于效果作战理论</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">基于效果作战理论是以色列在放弃系统作战设计方法后采用的作战理论，侧重于效果导向的作战规划。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="系统通论">
  <data key="d0">系统通论</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">系统通论是系统作战设计的理论基础之一，强调系统的整体性和开放性。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="复杂性理论">
  <data key="d0">复杂性理论</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">复杂性理论是系统作战设计的理论基础之一，用于分析复杂系统的行为和相互作用。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="基于任务重心的作战设计方法">
  <data key="d0">基于任务重心的作战设计方法</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">基于任务重心的作战设计方法亦称经典要素作战设计方法，由美国乔伊·斯特兰奇博士于1996年提出，以"重心-关键能力-关键需求-关键脆弱点"推理模型为基础。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="乔伊·斯特兰奇">
  <data key="d0">乔伊·斯特兰奇</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">乔伊·斯特兰奇是美国博士，于1996年提出了基于任务重心的作战设计方法。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="重心-关键能力-关键需求-关键脆弱点推理模型">
  <data key="d0">重心-关键能力-关键需求-关键脆弱点推理模型</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">重心-关键能力-关键需求-关键脆弱点推理模型是基于任务重心的作战设计方法的核心分析框架，用于确定作战重心和关键脆弱点。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="系统框架">
  <data key="d0">系统框架</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">系统框架是系统作战设计方法的组成部分，为学习和适应提供结构化的分析框架，包括敌方推论、指挥推论、后勤推论等内容。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="战役框架">
  <data key="d0">战役框架</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">战役框架是系统作战设计和战役筹划中的关键要素，用于确定战役的范围和目标。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad41c5f955e8f92f03f6d44d4fb9028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maritime Mobile Combat Forces">
  <data key="d0">Maritime Mobile Combat Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Maritime Mobile Combat Forces are naval units that conduct mobile combat operations and determine key strike targets and priorities based on designated combat sea areas and missions from joint campaign command organizations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Campaign Command Organization">
  <data key="d0">Joint Campaign Command Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint Campaign Command Organization is the authority that assigns combat sea areas and missions to maritime combat forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Joint campaign command organization refers to the unified command structure that coordinates military operations across different branches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac85adc8a2b85efe002961c570418c8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maritime Strike Operations">
  <data key="d0">Maritime Strike Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maritime Strike Operations are combat operations characterized by multiple strike methods and wide operational ranges, capable of executing various combat missions including long-range precision strikes from sea to land.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aircraft Carrier">
  <data key="d0">Aircraft Carrier</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Aircraft Carriers are large naval vessels that deploy carrier-based aircraft for air strikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface Warship">
  <data key="d0">Surface Warship</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface Warships are naval vessels capable of launching cruise missiles for sea and land strikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface warships are naval vessels that can launch cruise missiles against land targets, typically operating independently or in small formations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a99a4e73ad9a3b3dcf19a65e4699c53</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Submarine">
  <data key="d0">Submarine</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Submarines are underwater vessels that can launch cruise missiles for sea and land strikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Submarine refers to underwater vessels capable of conducting covert operations and attacks on enemy ships.&lt;SEP&gt;Submarines are underwater naval vessels capable of launching submarine-borne cruise missiles for ground attack operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2908bfab4991ca36f91164f7b6393526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cruise Missile">
  <data key="d0">Cruise Missile</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cruise missiles are portable, long-range weapons with good penetration performance, high accuracy, and strong destructive capability, typically launched from land, sea, underwater, or air platforms outside the combat zone.&lt;SEP&gt;A cruise missile is a type of missile that is smaller and faces increasing challenges to penetration capabilities from air defense technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Cruise Missiles are precision-guided weapons launched from naval platforms for striking sea and land targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Cruise missiles are shipborne or submarine-borne precision weapons used in ground attack operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bda4e71c2e2aedaec198d4b1d87ca5b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bcc2f01cacb5d64a03f00ef0877625a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Naval Combat Formation">
  <data key="d0">Naval Combat Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Naval Combat Formations are organized naval units that can be distributed along fire strike zones to conduct remote fire strikes from multiple campaign directions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maritime Mobile Forces">
  <data key="d0">Maritime Mobile Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Maritime Mobile Forces follow a four-phase combat process including planning, preparation, execution, and assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Operation Plan">
  <data key="d0">Combat Operation Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Operation Plans include conceptual planning (combat design) and detailed planning (action plans) covering combat progress, coordination, and force maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sea-To-Sea And Sea-To-Land Strike Operations">
  <data key="d0">Sea-To-Sea And Sea-To-Land Strike Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Sea-To-Sea And Sea-To-Land Strike Operations involve attacking enemy naval and land targets using通用platforms, weapons, and information systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air-Sea Integrated Operations">
  <data key="d0">Air-Sea Integrated Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Air-Sea Integrated Operations require unified planning, command, and coordinated actions for sea-to-sea and sea-to-land strikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire Strike Zone">
  <data key="d0">Fire Strike Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire Strike Zone is an area where multiple naval strike formations are distributed for conducting remote fire strikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sea Control">
  <data key="d0">Sea Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sea Control refers to the objective of dominating maritime areas and is pursued simultaneously with air and land control.&lt;SEP&gt;Sea control refers to the dominance or control over maritime areas, a key objective in naval warfare.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fafd99eac7a9f0a81e5f0af175de98</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Control">
  <data key="d0">Air Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Air Control refers to the objective of dominating airspace and is pursued simultaneously with sea and land control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Land Control">
  <data key="d0">Land Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Land Control refers to the objective of dominating land areas and is pursued simultaneously with sea and air control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Home Port Base">
  <data key="d0">Home Port Base</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Home Port Base is the logistical support facility for naval forces, difficult to supply from when conducting deep sea mobile operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-003a5d2c8802dfadf15c1edad5131699</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maritime Battlefield">
  <data key="d0">Maritime Battlefield</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Maritime Battlefield is the operational environment where naval forces execute missions based on situational awareness.</data>
