<node id="Functional Domain Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Functional Domain Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Functional Domain Analysis is a process within Mission Capability Description that identifies operational tasks, conditions, and standards needed to achieve operational goals based on national military strategy and joint operation concepts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5c0970b8c1b0e778f4a08b68650be23</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Requirements Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Functional Requirements Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Functional Requirements Analysis is a process within Mission Capability Description that evaluates future operational capabilities and current capabilities to identify gaps and develop time frames for solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5c0970b8c1b0e778f4a08b68650be23</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="侦察能力">
  <data key="d0">侦察能力</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reconnaissance capability refers to the ability to conduct intelligence gathering and surveillance operations, assessed based on current reconnaissance status and mission requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="侦察监视计划">
  <data key="d0">侦察监视计划</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reconnaissance and surveillance plan is a method for organizing intelligence reconnaissance actions, developed based on intelligence requirements and matched with reconnaissance and surveillance platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="情报信息">
  <data key="d0">情报信息</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Intelligence information refers to processed and evaluated data obtained from reconnaissance operations, which is distributed after screening and assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;情报信息是通过情报手段获取的各种数据资料，包括关键信息需求、作战意图、打击目标、作战任务等相关内容。&lt;SEP&gt;情报信息是经过验证的情报数据和内容，可以是原始信息或经过分析加工的情报产品。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-016b122f52ce767ff6277d5f69a238ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f07896e22c4755245b43471a9c4d9500</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="火力打击">
  <data key="d0">火力打击</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">火力打击是作战任务的类型之一，用于对敌方目标实施攻击。&lt;SEP&gt;Firepower strike is the application of military force against selected targets, requiring matching with appropriate weapons and forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2aa6fbd1f527b7422a45710c2b7351</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="目标整编">
  <data key="d0">目标整编</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Target organization refers to the process of integrating and ranking strike targets, forming target lists and determining attack sequence and expected effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="打击计划">
  <data key="d0">打击计划</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strike plan refers to the operational plan for executing attacks against targets, including allocation of firepower and task forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="任务分配">
  <data key="d0">任务分配</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Task allocation refers to the process of distributing strike missions to task forces based on battlefield situation and target changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="部队">
  <data key="d0">部队</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The troops whose actions are commanded, controlled, and tracked during campaign implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Troops or forces refer to military units assigned to execute strike missions, whose capability and status must be evaluated for mission feasibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Troops are military units that receive combat orders and carry out combat missions under command and control.&lt;SEP&gt;部队是军事系统中的作战力量组织。</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ed84de6534558d8934cfe16642690e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9462b55eac26353ece0a6caed0d12c93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f07896e22c4755245b43471a9c4d9500&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b0ab60a625810ad5c7b928b03f9f35b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
