</node>
<node id="Navy Policies And Procedures">
  <data key="d0">Navy Policies And Procedures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Navy Policies and Procedures (NPP) is the naval combat mission planning process used for operational planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="US Navy Mission Planning Process">
  <data key="d0">US Navy Mission Planning Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">US Navy mission planning process follows a six-step approach including mission analysis, course of action development, analysis, comparison and decision, plan and order preparation, and transition.&lt;SEP&gt;The US Navy Mission Planning Process is a systematic approach for developing combat plans, consisting of multiple phases from plan generation to execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f1759230375668c37a3de633d934a17</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Mission Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mission Analysis clarifies task objectives, methods, possibilities, and risks to establish a common understanding of the mission.&lt;SEP&gt;Mission analysis is the first step in US Navy mission planning, aimed at helping commanders and staff understand current situations and generate mission statements.&lt;SEP&gt;Mission Analysis is the second step in network attack and defense planning, involving understanding the mission objectives and conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Mission analysis is the process of examining and evaluating military missions, assumptions, and reports for authenticity and feasibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03367b3f7f20f2a9f77e53026ed67d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92553208105fab6dba3a8603376ed607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed702044df254afe00f3e24e778f48f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Course Of Action Development">
  <data key="d0">Course Of Action Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Course of action development is the second step in US Navy mission planning, where multiple operational plans are developed based on mission statements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deliberate Action Planning">
  <data key="d0">Deliberate Action Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deliberate action planning is a mode of operational planning used when mission planning time is not limited, for developing future combat plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1778766756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crisis Action Planning">
  <data key="d0">Crisis Action Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The US Military equivalent of Pre-war Plan, formulated when crisis events are anticipated or occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Crisis action planning is a mode of operational planning used when mission planning time is critical, to respond to specific battlefield events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38e9493e7a7348c2d48edb6be9c328ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b0ab60a625810ad5c7b928b03f9f35b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
